Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||12-13-2001||05:38 PM||||Hey guys, <BR> I have changed my rear brake pads, and fronts. I dont know what the bleeder valve looks like. Does anyone have a picture of what it looks like on the brakes? On the last two break jobs, I changed the pads, then just lived with a spungy pedal until the air is slowly pumped outta the lines. What is the procedure to bleeding the brakes?||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-13-2001||09:34 PM||||Are you sure you need to bleed?  (The brakes, I mean.)  If you only changed the pads, you shouldn't have gotten air into the hydraulic system.<P>Check the brake articles in Ogre's cave.  Maybe the parking brakes need to be adjusted.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||solo2m4||12-13-2001||09:45 PM||||On my frist fiero the same thing happened frist time it went away after I bleed the brakes second time It came back so I changed the brake fluid and the prob never came back.<BR>I don't know if that will help you, but brake fluid dose not cost much!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-13-2001||10:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Johnson's85SE:<BR><B> I changed the pads, then just lived with a spungy pedal until the air is slowly pumped outta the lines. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE></B><P>That should NOT happen, all hydraulic systems are supposed to be air tight, only the fluid must be present in the lines.  If you can "pump air out of the system", then you can also let in air and pump out fluid.  Something here dosent make sense.<P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><P>What is the procedure to bleeding the brakes?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you are going to be doing projects like these yourself on your car and it is your first time, invest in a Haynes manual.  They are around $15 at most auto parts places, and they give a lot of information to someone new to working on cars.  They will describe how to bleed the brakes, and explain a lot of other things about brakes too.<BR>||||reg||1
